---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Booker from '../components/Booker.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const { email, brand, brandFull, logo, logoAlt } = site;
const mailto = `mailto:${email}`;
const title = `Privacy Policy — ${brandFull}`;
const description =
  'How Anno Domini collects, uses, and stores the personal data you provide when you contact us, and your rights under UK data protection law.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <!-- Minimal nav: this page has no hero, so the bar stays frosted. The logo and
       "Back to site" both return to the homepage; the theme toggle reuses the
       shared #modeToggle wiring from scripts/theme.ts. -->
  <nav class="nav scrolled" id="nav" data-screen-label="Nav">
    <a class="os-mark" href="/" aria-label={brand}><img class="os-mark__img" src={logo} alt={logoAlt} /></a>
    <div class="nav-center"></div>
    <div class="nav-right">
      <a class="btn" href="/"><span class="mk">&larr;</span> Back to site</a>
      <button class="nav-toggle" id="modeToggle" aria-label="Toggle light and dark">
        <svg class="sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"></circle><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4"></path></svg>
        <svg class="moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12.8A9 9 0 1 1 11.2 3a7 7 0 0 0 9.8 9.8z"></path></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <span id="top"></span>

  <main class="band wrap legal-main">
    <article class="legal inner">
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated body">Last updated: [DATE — set on launch]</p>

      <!-- Owner note: remove once the remaining legal-identity placeholders are
           filled. Collection method and processors below are now accurate. -->
      <div class="draft-note">
        <strong>Note for the site owner — remove before launch.</strong>
        Still to fill in: <strong>legal/trading name</strong>, <strong>company number</strong>
        (if registered), <strong>registered/postal address</strong>, the
        <strong>retention period</strong> in §6, and the “Last updated” date above. The
        contact email, the contact-form description, the Web3Forms processor disclosure, and
        the ICO details are already correct.
      </div>

      <p>This policy explains what personal data we collect when you contact us through this
      website, how we use and store it, and the rights you have under UK data protection law
      (the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018).</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p><strong>[COMPANY LEGAL NAME]</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”), [COMPANY NUMBER — if a
      registered company], of [REGISTERED / POSTAL ADDRESS], is the <strong>data
      controller</strong> responsible for your personal data. If you have any questions about
      this policy or your data, contact us at <a href={mailto}>{email}</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. What personal data we collect</h2>
      <p>We only collect the information you choose to give us. When you submit our on-site
      contact form (the “Start a conversation” panel), we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your <strong>name</strong>;</li>
        <li>your <strong>email address</strong>;</li>
        <li>the contents of your <strong>message</strong> and any details you choose to include.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you email us directly instead, we receive whatever information your message
      contains. We do not collect special category data, and we do not use tracking or
      advertising cookies (see “Cookies and local storage” below).</p>

      <h2>3. How we use it, and our lawful basis</h2>
      <p>We use this information to respond to your enquiry, to discuss whether and how we can
      work together, and to keep a record of our correspondence.</p>
      <p>Our lawful basis for this processing is <strong>legitimate interests</strong> —
      namely, responding to people who contact us about our services. Where you contact us
      with a view to engaging us, we also rely on <strong>taking steps at your request before
      entering into a contract</strong>. We do not use your details for marketing unless you
      have separately and explicitly agreed to it.</p>

      <h2>4. How it reaches us, and how we store it</h2>
      <p>When you submit the contact form, your details are transmitted to us by
      <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, a form-to-email delivery service that acts as our data
      processor solely to forward your message to our inbox. We then hold your information
      securely within <strong>Google Workspace</strong>, which also acts as a data processor
      and stores the data on our behalf under a data processing agreement.</p>
      <p>Some of this processing may take place outside the UK; where it does, it is protected
      by an adequacy decision or by appropriate safeguards (such as the UK International Data
      Transfer Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses). We apply reasonable technical
      and organisational measures to keep your data secure.</p>

      <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We share your personal data only with the service providers that help us run our
      business (such as Web3Forms and Google, as described above), acting on our instructions,
      or where we are required to do so by law. <strong>We do not sell, rent, or trade your
      personal data to anyone.</strong></p>

      <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep your information only for as long as we need it for the purposes above —
      [RETENTION PERIOD — suggested: up to 24 months after our last contact, unless an ongoing
      relationship means we need to keep it longer]. After that, we securely delete it.</p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>be informed about how we use your data (this notice);</li>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
        <li>have your data erased;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to our processing of your data;</li>
        <li>data portability;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, where our processing relies on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, email us at <a href={mailto}>{email}</a>. We will
      respond within one month.</p>

      <h2>8. Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>This website does not use tracking or advertising cookies. It stores a single
      functional preference in your browser (your light/dark theme choice) so the site
      remembers how you like to view it. This is not used to identify or track you.</p>

      <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you have a concern about how we handle your personal data, please contact us first
      so we can try to put it right. You also have the right to complain to the UK regulator,
      the <strong>Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO)</strong>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>online at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a></li>
        <li>by phone on 0303 123 1113</li>
        <li>by post to Information Commissioner’s Office, Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire, SK9 5AF</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page,
      and the “Last updated” date above will show the latest version.</p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
  <Booker />
</Base>

<style>
  /* Page-scoped legal-prose rhythm. Uses the shared semantic tokens so the
     notice inherits light/dark theming from os-site.css automatically. */
  .legal-main { padding-top: clamp(140px, 18vh, 220px); }
  .legal { max-width: 72ch; }
  .legal__title { font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 60px); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .legal__updated { margin-bottom: clamp(34px, 5vh, 56px); color: var(--ink-mute); }
  .legal h2 {
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 116, 'wght' 540;
    font-size: clamp(19px, 1.9vw, 25px);
    line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    margin: clamp(34px, 5vh, 52px) 0 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .legal p, .legal li {
    font-size: clamp(15.5px, 1.12vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.74; color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 100, 'wght' 400;
  }
  .legal p + p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .legal ul { margin: 12px 0 0; padding-left: 1.25em; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .legal a:hover { opacity: 0.7; }
  .legal strong { font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 104, 'wght' 600; color: var(--ink); }

  /* Visible "fill these in" banner — for the site owner, remove once live. */
  .draft-note {
    margin-bottom: clamp(34px, 5vh, 52px);
    padding: 18px 22px; border-radius: 8px;
    border: var(--hair-w) dashed var(--accent-warm);
    background: var(--bleed);
    font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .draft-note strong { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
